// Two tests whose names share no substring, so `--filter=square` is a question with exactly one
// answer.
//
// ⭐ THE UNSELECTED TEST WOULD FAIL IF IT RAN, and that is the fixture's whole point. Against two
// passing tests, a filter that quietly selected both would differ from a working one only in lines
// nobody reads and not in the exit code; against this one it is a red run.
typealias Length = int(0 to i64.max)

function perimeter(side Length) returns Length
	return side * 4
end 'perimeter'

test 'a square has four equal sides'
	try Expect.equal(perimeter(3) as AssertedInt, expected: 12)
end 'a square has four equal sides'

test 'the unselected one would FAIL if the filter let it run'
	try Expect.equal(perimeter(3) as AssertedInt, expected: 99)
end 'the unselected one would FAIL if the filter let it run'
